% Zitieren mit automatischem 'Ref.' davor:
\RequirePackage[style=numeric]{biblatex}
\RequirePackage{xstring}
\RequirePackage{letltxmacro}

\LetLtxMacro\origcite\cite
\NewDocumentCommand{\refcite}{om}{%
	\begingroup%
	\def\tempx{0}%
	\StrCount{#2}{,}[\tempx]% Zählt die Anzahl der Kommas in der ref aufzaehlung. Sobald eins auftaucht wird aus Ref., Refs..
	\ifnum\tempx > 0%
	Refs. %
	\else%
	Ref. %
	\fi%
	\endgroup%
	\IfNoValueTF{#1}% You might be wondering why we need the ‘{}c after ‘O’ when there is no default value: why not just ‘o’? Well, there is ‘o’ as well. Unlike \newcommand, \NewDocumentCommand can tell the difference between an option argument that is not given and one that is empty. To do that, it provides a test to see if the argument is empty: \IfNoValueTF
	{% arg 1 not given
		\origcite{#2}%
	}
	{%
		\origcite[#1]{#2}%
	}%
}

